        "runId": "ada-en-mw63klk3-vv0roc62-amanda",
        "model": "GPT-6.1",
        "wordAbsenceReason": "The Word splits this route across Days 6 and 7, includes an intervening Wine & Spa stay, and lacks the church description. No Word passage covers this current direct-transfer itinerary block."
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, transfer to the airport for your flight to Porto Alegre. On arrival, continue to Gramado.\n\nGramado looks quite different from the Brazil you may be used to. Its architecture recalls both a German town and a Swiss mountain village. The city is known for its chocolate, restaurants, small boutiques and chalet-style hotels.\n\nOnce you’ve checked in, you can stroll along the quiet streets, have lunch at a local restaurant and explore the town. The main square is home to Igreja Matriz São Pedro, built from 78,000 basalt stones and decorated with stained-glass scenes from the life of Saint Peter. Twelve life-size statues of the apostles stand in front of the church."
    },
